{"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"In machine learning workflows, deterministic reproducibility is vital for auditing, hyperparameter tuning, and regression testing. SwiftSci provides:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Xoshiro256++ Generator","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":": A modern, high-throughput pseudo-random number generator conforming to standard "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RandomNumberGenerator"},{"type":"text","text":" with period $2^{256} - 1$ passing BigCrush."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"code":"randomState","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" Parameter Propagation","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Standardized "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"randomState: Int?"},{"type":"text","text":" parameters across ensemble estimators ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftML\/documentation\/SwiftML\/RandomForestClassifier"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftML\/documentation\/SwiftML\/RandomForestRegressor"},{"type":"text","text":") and clustering models ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KMeans"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Deterministic Parallel Construction","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Fixed-order tree compilation preserving deterministic tie-breaking even under multi-threaded Swift Concurrency execution ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TaskGroup"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"orderedList"},{"anchor":"1-Using-randomState-in-Random-Forests","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"1. Using `randomState` in Random Forests"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Pass an integer ","type":"tex